  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CONSERVACION Y RESTAURACION DE SITIOS INVERNALES EGRETTA RUFESCENS MX II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partners will advance conservation and protection activities, in some of the areas previously identified in the first phase, and will begin to work in the wetlands of the Northeast coast of Yucatan, that support wintering populations arriving from Florida. Based on information that was generated during the first phase, especially results from the first year of monitoring, they will (1) establish a long-term conservation agreement for the protection of 3,300 hectares of reddish Egret habitat within the lands owned by the Salinera Exportadora de Sal, which are adjacent to the Laguna Ojo de Liebre in Baja California Sur; and commence the process to obtain the concession of 200 ha of mangrove habitat in Laguna Mar Muerto, Oaxaca for the protection of reddish egret; (2) Develop a management plan for 20,000 ha of wetlands adjacent to the Laguna Ojo de Liebre, within the lands of Salinera Exportadora de Sal; (3) Reforest 100 ha of mangrove in Laguna Madre, Tamaulipas, and restore 200 ha of mangrove in Laguna Mar Muerto, through reestablishment of adequate hydrologic flow regimes; (4) Control and extraction of feral animals from the northern islands of Laguna Madre, Tamaulipas; (5) Monitor specific reddish egret populations and their habitat at specific sites in Mexico; (6) Based on Open Standards, develop a Business Plan for the Conservation of the Reddish Egret in Mexico; (7) Develop outreach and community education in areas where human disturbance has been identified as a major threat.</narrative>
  </description>
